# DocAtlas core rules

This project uses DocAtlas (https://github.com/JeeEko/DocAtlas) for documentation.

## Before making changes

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `doc-atlas/docs/START_HERE.md`
2. Check `doc-atlas/docs/` for architecture, onboarding, and runbook context
3. If behavior changes, plan doc updates in the same change

## Documentation standards

- Write in plain English for developers new to this repo
- Use confidence tags: `[verified]`, `[likely]`, `[uncertain]`, `[planned]`
- Do not mark content `[verified]` unless confirmed against code or tests
- Replace `TODO` and `TBD` placeholders when you fill in content

## Drift prevention

- Run `docatlas drift` after doc changes
- Update `doc-atlas/docs/GLOSSARY.md` when introducing new domain terms
- Keep `doc-atlas/docs/RUNBOOK.md` commands copy-paste accurate

## Do not

- Invent features not in the codebase
- Skip doc updates for user-facing behavior changes
- Delete existing documentation without team reason
